# Scoring determinism

Pure functions only. No I/O, no network, no clock, no randomness, no model calls.

- The same input MUST produce byte-identical output.
- Each characteristic starts at 100; findings apply penalties stated in `docs/SCORING.md`.
- Implementation and `docs/SCORING.md` must agree. Change both in the same commit.
- An active accepted decision suppresses its penalty and is recorded in `suppressedBy`. Suppression is always visible, never silent.
- Every scoring change needs a fixture in `fixtures/` demonstrating it.
